  <dsc><c id="32b7364e72a75c69273af1defe977983" level="series"><did><unittitle>Subject files</unittitle><unitid>1</unitid><unitid type="aspace_uri">/repositories/2/archival_objects/1313702</unitid><physdesc altrender="whole"><extent altrender="materialtype spaceoccupied">4.7 Cubic Feet</extent><extent altrender="carrier">10 document boxes: 10 legal boxes</extent></physdesc><unitdate datechar="creation" normal="1970/1982" type="inclusive">1970-1982</unitdate></did><scopecontent id="f979c452238a1d7da43d5c49c3080ca9"><head>Scope and Contents</head><p>This series contains subject files created and maintained by the Ford Foundation's Regional Office for West Africa. Subject files document the West Africa Office's programming between the 1970s and 1980s. </p><p>Files provide insight into the organizational history of the West Africa Program during this time period. The program was managed by a regional office in Lagos, Nigeria, and for several years in the 1970s, the Lagos Office maintained a suboffice in Abidjan, Cote d'Ivoire (Ivory Coast). Materials in the series show the Lagos and Abidjan Offices working together on the West Africa Program's support for Francophone West African countries like Cote d'Ivoire and Mali. The series documents the West Africa Office's prioritizing of both Nigeria and Francophone West African countries. </p><p>The Ford Foundation's support for education, agriculture, and family planning is documented in the series. Education programming centers around the Francophone West Africa Education Research Training Program, and files highlight the work of Ralph Harbison, Assistant Representative and Program Advisor in Education.  </p><p>Materials related to agriculture regard food production, farming systems, livestock planning, natural resources, and rural development. The agricultural programming specific to Nigeria that is documented in the series is largely connected to Nigeria's Third National Development Plan for agriculture that was supported by Ford Foundation grant 07300620 to the Federal Republic of Nigeria. </p><p>The Foundation's concern for rural development intersected with its programming for family planning as demonstrated by the Rural Maternal and Child Health/Family Planning Program. Files also show the influence of a population program lens on the Foundation's support for family planning. Much of this work was managed by Oyewole P. Owolabi, Health and Population Projects Coordinator.</p></scopecontent><c id="3c56385f4c6ecd847144dacb1792551d" level="file"><did><unittitle>Francophone West Africa Education Research Training Program - Reports and papers</unittitle><unitid type="aspace_uri">/repositories/2/archival_objects/1313703</unitid><unitdate datechar="creation" normal="1974/1980" type="inclusive">1974-1980</unitdate><container altrender="Legal Document Box" id="7f36911508fb354dd15120c20f333a07" label="mixed materials [A0000000128575]" type="box">1</container><container id="29e29ddeed7ee21e1521effc5ffa0914" parent="7f36911508fb354dd15120c20f333a07" type="folder">1-3</container></did></c><c id="3ed441b8faf45af4290e607d3d8b11be" level="file"><did><unittitle>Francophone West Africa Education Research Training Program - Universite Laval</unittitle><unitid type="aspace_uri">/repositories/2/archival_objects/1313704</unitid><unitdate datechar="creation" normal="1974/1975" type="inclusive">1974-1975</unitdate><container altrender="Legal Document Box" id="8ccfcf85cac6ee118069c3f1d17cd8ea" label="mixed materials [A0000000128575]" type="box">1</container><container id="751b18b9821a0c6ccea3f39d3cca220c" parent="8ccfcf85cac6ee118069c3f1d17cd8ea" type="folder">4</container><container altrender="Legal Document Box" id="08c0807700857f75b9c3253efc56d9fd" label="mixed materials [A0000000128576]" type="box">2</container><container id="e9c86f0b79bd08614e71a7435247a1ed" parent="08c0807700857f75b9c3253efc56d9fd" type="folder">5</container></did><scopecontent id="36f0bceb522e69084e3e6af29ddabb4b"><head>Scope and Co